Description: Wild OS slim headers: menus in a hamburger menu, no menu bar
 A KDE app's window stacks a title bar, a menu bar and a toolbar, which
 makes its header much taller than Wild OS's own apps. Here every window
 with a menu bar and a toolbar has a hamburger menu first on its toolbar
 (the app's own, moved there, or one KXmlGui adds) holding the
 same menus, and starts without its menu bar. Windows without a toolbar
 keep their menu bar, so no menu is ever out of reach. A menu bar shown
 or hidden by hand is remembered.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

